sentences.l:
So they, on the one hand, such things to one another were speaking,
and upon Aeneas rushed Diomedes, good at the war-cry,
knowing that over him Apollo himself was holding his hands;

sentences.t:
Ἆρες Ἄρες βροτολοιγὲ μιαιφόνε τειχεσιπλῆτα,
οὐκ ἂν δὴ τόνδ’ ἄνδρα μάχης ἐρύσαιο μετελθὼν
Τυδεΐδην, ὃς νῦν γε καὶ ἂν Διὶ πατρὶ μάχοιτο;

sentences.l:
So having spoken, he himself sat down on high Pergamus,
and the Trojan ranks ruinous Ares urged on, going among them,
making himself like swift Acamas, leader of the Thracians;

for far away is Lycia, by eddying Xanthus,
where my dear wife I left and my infant son,
and behind many possessions, which whoever is in need longs for.

and around them night
impetuous Ares enfolded, over the battle, helping the Trojans,
going about everywhere;

and they were glad,
when they saw him both alive and unharmed, coming near,
and having good might;
